[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

This is an unofficial [B]LineageOS 11 (Android 4.4.4 KitKat)[/B] build for the [B]LG G2 Mini LTE D625[/B] (codename [B]g2mv[/B]). It is the first custom ROM for this model, which uses an [B]NVIDIA Tegra 4i[/B] instead of a Snapdragon, so nothing from the D620/D618 ports applies to it.

The kernel is built from LG's GPL source with fixes for this ROM (backlight, proximity, flash, KnockON, live battery voltage). Proprietary files come from stock firmware D62510c. Every result listed below was checked on real hardware with this kernel.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for the Tegra 4i D625. It will not boot on the Snapdragon G2 Mini models (D620, D618...).[/B][/COLOR]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Requires the patched bootloader and TWRP:[/B][/COLOR]
[LIST=1]
[*][URL="PUT_BOOTLOADER_GUIDE_URL_HERE"][GUIDE] How To Unlock the Bootloader LG G2 Mini LTE D625 (Tegra 4i)[/URL]
[*][URL="PUT_TWRP_THREAD_URL_HERE"][RECOVERY][UNOFFICIAL] TWRP 3.1.1-1 for LG G2 Mini LTE D625[/URL]
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Device specs[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG G2 Mini LTE (LG-D625), codename g2mv
[*]Android version: 4.4.4 KitKat (LineageOS 11, the LineageOS-maintained cm-11.0 branch with later security patches)
[*]Kernel: Linux 3.4.65, compiled from source (pda_android_defconfig)
[*]SoC: NVIDIA Tegra 4i (T148), quad-core ARM Cortex-A9 up to 1.73 GHz
[*]GPU: NVIDIA ULP GeForce (OpenGL ES 2.0), up to 595 MHz
[*]RAM: 1 GB
[*]Display: 4.7 inch, 540x960, 60 Hz
[*]Modem: NVIDIA Icera (2G/3G/LTE)
[*]Base firmware: D62510c (Android 4.4.2)
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status: Beta[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read the known issues before flashing.[/B][/COLOR] This is a first public build. Everything in the list below was tested, but a few items still need a field test.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot:[/B] boots to the launcher in about 15-25 s, including the first boot after a clean install.
[*][B]Display and HW acceleration:[/B] NVIDIA GLES driver and hwcomposer overlays. The RT8542 backlight is controlled by the ROM. Auto-brightness works. GPU performance matches the LG stock ROM (79 FPS vs 78.6 FPS in the same 1280x720 test scene).
[*][B]Touch:[/B] multitouch, with an on-screen navigation bar.
[*][B]KnockON (double tap to wake):[/B] toggle in Settings > Display. It wakes from deep sleep and is blocked when the proximity sensor is covered (pocket).
[*][B]Calls, SMS and SIM:[/B] Icera modem, voice calls, SMS and HSPA+ data (tested on Claro Peru). The in-call proximity sensor turns the screen off at your ear. Incoming calls wake the phone from deep sleep.
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] Broadcom bcmdhd, WPA2.
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] BCM4334, scan, pairing and file transfer.
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, earpiece, headset and microphone, using the stock NVIDIA audio HAL.
[*][B]Camera:[/B] photos and flash. Video recording at stock quality: [B]1080p at 17 Mbps[/B] on the back camera (with stabilization) and 720p at 12 Mbps on the front camera. Gallery thumbnails and hardware video playback.
[*][B]Torch:[/B] works from the Torch app and as video light. The LED switches off when the camera closes.
[*][B]Sensors:[/B] accelerometer, magnetometer, proximity and light.
[*][B]Vibrator:[/B] max77660 haptics.
[*][B]Deep sleep:[/B] Tegra LP0 suspend. The modem wakes the phone for calls and SMS.
[*][B]Offline charging:[/B] stock LG charge animation when the phone is off; Power boots Android.
[*][B]NFC:[/B] PN547 controller. Android Beam between two phones works (photo sent over NFC + Bluetooth).
[*][B]IR blaster:[/B] standard Android ConsumerIr support, so any IR remote app that uses the Android API can use it. The stock LG QuickRemote app also works.
[*][B]GPS:[/B] BCM4752 with AGPS (SUPL) and LTO orbit data download.
[*][B]NVIDIA power management:[/B] powerservice and ussrd run as on stock, with the interactive CPU governor.
[*][B]Root:[/B] built-in superuser (Settings > Developer options > Root access).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Incoming calls while the phone sleeps can be missed in weak coverage.[/B] In poor signal the modem sometimes loses network registration while the CPU is in deep sleep, and the network never pages it. With good signal, calls come in from deep sleep.
[*][B]LTE (4G):[/B] enabled (preferred network LTE/WCDMA/GSM, selectable in Settings), but a 4G connection is not confirmed yet. There is no LTE coverage at the test location: the LG stock ROM also stays on 3G (HSPA+) there. If you have 4G coverage, please report whether you get LTE.
[*][B]GPS:[/B] the chip, AGPS and orbit data work, but an outdoor satellite fix is not confirmed yet (0 satellites indoors).
[*][B]NFC:[/B] reading a tag or card is not tested yet (Android Beam is).
[*][B]IR blaster:[/B] the LED was checked with a camera; controlling a real TV is not tested yet.
[*][B]Location without Google services:[/B] there is no network location provider, only GPS. The lock screen weather widget therefore uses GPS for its location, limited to 60 seconds and at most once per hour. You can also set a fixed city in its settings.
[/LIST]

